1744032100000|can machines ever be conscious|Hard problem of consciousness (Chalmers). If consciousness emerges from complexity, future AGI *might* experience qualia—but we lack ways to test this.|0|philosophy,AI  
1744032200000|what were Kenya's earliest civilizations|Kenya's earliest inhabitants were hunter-gatherers like the Khoisan. By 1000 BCE, Bantu migrants (e.g., Kikuyu, Luhya) introduced farming. Coastal city-states (e.g., Mombasa, Malindi) thrived via Indian Ocean trade with Arabs, Persians, and Chinese.|0|history,precolonial
1744032300000|who built Swahili culture|Swahili culture emerged from 8th-century interactions between Bantu Africans, Arab traders, and Persian settlers. It blended Bantu languages with Arabic, creating Kiswahili and unique architecture (e.g., Gedi Ruins).|0|culture,history
1744032400000|what was the Maasai's role in pre-colonial Kenya|The Maasai (Nilotic migrants) dominated Kenya's Rift Valley by 1700s as pastoralists. They resisted slavery and influenced regional trade with their cattle-based economy.|0|history,tribes
1744032500000|how did British colonization begin in Kenya|The British East Africa Company took control in 1885, building the Uganda Railway (1896-1901) ("Lunatic Express"). Kenya became a British crown colony in 1920, displacing natives for white settlers.|0|history,colonialism
1744032600000|what was the Mau Mau uprising|Mau Mau (1952–1960) was a violent anti-colonial rebellion by Kikuyu farmers against British land seizures. 11,000 rebels died; Britain jailed leaders like Dedan Kimathi but accelerated independence.|0|history,resistance
1744032700000|who were Kenya's independence heroes|Jomo Kenyatta (1st president), Tom Mboya (labor leader), and Oginga Odinga (vice president). Kenyatta’s 1963 slogan "Harambee" ("Pull together") unified the nation.|0|history,independence
1744032800000|what happened after Kenya's independence in 1963|Kenyatta promoted capitalism but centralized power. Daniel arap Moi (1978–2002) ruled dictatorially under a one-party system until protests forced multi-party elections in 1991.|0|history,politics
1744032900000|what caused the 2007–2008 Kenyan crisis|Disputed elections triggered ethnic violence (1,200+ died). The ICC charged leaders (e.g., Uhuru Kenyatta) with crimes against humanity. Power-sharing (Kibaki + Odinga) ended the crisis.|0|history,conflict
1744033000000|what is Kenya's 2010 constitution|It decentralized power, created 47 counties, and added a Bill of Rights. Landmark reforms: gender equity (no >2/3 single-gender gov’t) and environmental protections.|0|history,law
1744033100000|how did Swahili become Kenya's lingua franca|British colonizers promoted it to unify diverse tribes. Post-independence, it symbolized pan-Africanism (e.g., "Harambee" is Swahili). Now taught in schools alongside English.|0|culture,language
1744033200000|why is Kenya an tech hub|Pioneered mobile money (M-Pesa, 2007). Silicon Savannah (Nairobi) thrives due to cheap internet, startups like Ushahidi, and coding bootcamps (e.g., Moringa School).|0|economy,technology
1744033300000|what is Kenya's Great Rift Valley|A geological trench stretching 6,000 km. Home to early hominid fossils (e.g., Turkana Boy, 1.6M yrs old) and UNESCO sites like Lake Nakuru’s flamingos.|0|geography,history
1744033400000|who was Wangari Maathai|Nobel Prize winner (2004) who founded the Green Belt Movement, planting 50M+ trees to combat deforestation. Jailed for opposing Moi’s regime.|0|history,environment
1744033500000|who is Ngũgĩ wa Thiong'o|Kenya’s famed writer (e.g., "Decolonising the Mind") who rejected English to write in Kikuyu. Exiled in 1982 for critiquing dictatorship.|0|culture,literature
1744033600000|should Kenya repatriate colonial-era artifacts|Pros: Reclaim cultural heritage (e.g., Ngai Ndeithia’s stolen art). Cons: Some argue museums like Britain’s preserve artifacts better.|0|history,debate
1744033700000|did British colonialism benefit Kenya|Mixed legacy: Built infrastructure (railways) but caused land dispossession and ethnic divisions. GDP grew post-independence (6% avg since 2010).|0|history,economics